readme.fair:
For a program that does not branch on its floats, ticks are a function of the program, so they have to match exactly. Scores pass through each machine's BLAS, so they can differ in the last digits. Same seeds of `{fair_entry}`, each machine against {fair_reference}, with a tolerance of {tolerance} fixed before the machines ran:

{fair_table}

The largest difference is {fair_max} bits per byte, about {fair_ratio} times below the record margin of 0.002. {branch_note} Rerun the comparison with `python tools/fairness.py study/fairness/logs/*.json`, or run the matrix yourself with [the fairness workflow](.github/workflows/fairness.yml) and download its artifacts. In a browser the demo reads the same tick as native code.
